From 67ca96940b52447402400ea804597c2c74ff45c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 09:25:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CRSF: add IMU telemetry frame with integrated gyro/acc
 increments

Adds an optional CRSF telemetry frame that carries batched delta-angle
(gyro) and delta-velocity (accelerometer) increments, integrated in the
PID loop, for visual-inertial odometry on the ground.

- telemetry/crsf_imu.c/.h: new PG_CRSF_IMU_CONFIG (559), accumulator
  (multiply-add per PID loop, rounding residual carried over so the sum
  never drifts, clipping flagged), single "ready" frame buffer where the
  newest frame wins, and the extended-header frame serializer.
- fc/core.c: accumulate after the motor update when enabled.
- telemetry/crsf.c: IMU frames go ahead of the regular schedule without
  resetting its timing; while IMU telemetry runs, regular frames are
  divided by crsf_imu_std_tlm_div (heartbeats keep their slots with V3).
- CLI: crsf_imu_telemetry, crsf_imu_interval_us, crsf_imu_batch,
  crsf_imu_accel (OFF/ON/FRAME), crsf_imu_frame_type, crsf_imu_std_tlm_div.
  Default OFF: no frame is built and the regular schedule is unchanged.
- Unit tests for encoding, integration, saturation, sequence/drops and
  schedule (with and without CRSF V3).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Leo8n1DewWe3nBjGiRLMvS
